  "detail": "retryFailures now keeps cfg.setup whenever a runner is passed (lines 283 and 306), but a runner doesn't mean a fresh checkout: the engine's baseline and regression retries and the land queue's local retries all pass one and run in the first attempt's checkout. Rerunning setup there can invalidate output an earlier, passing check produced. For example, setup cleans dist, a build check recreates it, and a test fails transiently. The retry cleans dist again and reruns only the test, so a transient failure becomes a persistent one. The engine comment 'Retry before resetting, so a check sees the same build output as its first attempt' relies on that not happening. Keep setup only when the retry may run in a different checkout, i.e. when it goes through an executor that gives each job its own checkout (the LAN executor for a repository in [workers] repos), the case the removed runGateExecution workaround handled. Local retries keep setup: []. Use one rule for the land queue and the engine paths, and add a local-retry test with a setup that removes an earlier check's output, asserting the retry doesn't rerun it."
